  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vitthal Kumar vs State on 7 November, 2017 Author: Pushpendra Singh Bhati Bench: Pushpendra Singh Bhati High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Criminal Misc(Pet.) No. 3609 / 2017 Kamlesh Kumar Son of Shri Dinesh Kumar, By Caste Agarwal, Resident of Adarsh Colony, Sumerpur, District Pali (Raj.) ----Petitioner Versus The State of Rajasthan ----Respondent Connected With S.B. Criminal Misc(Pet.) No. 3375 / 2017 Vitthal Kumar Son of Shri Dinesh Kumar, By Caste Agarwal, Resident of Sumerpur, District Pali (Raj.) ----Petitioner Versus State of Rajasthan ----Respondent _____________________________________________________ For Petitioner(s) : Mr. T.C. Sharma For Respondent(s) : Mr. V.S. Rajpurohit, Pp _____________________________________________________ Hon'Ble Dr. Justice Pushpendra Singh Bhati Order 07/11/2017 1.",
    "facts": "The petitioners have preferred these criminal misc. petitions under Sections 482 Cr.P.C. for quashing of FIR No.376/2017 registered at Police Station Sumerpur, Pali for the offences under Sections 420, 272, 273, 486, 487 of IPC and Section 3 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 and Section 102, 103, 104 of Business and Trademark Act, 1958. 2. This Court had earlier passed an order dated 11.10.2017 which reads as under: (2 of 3) [ CRLMP-3609/2017] \"The petitioner is directed to join the investigation and cooperate in the investigation. Put up on 01.11.2017, as prayed. 1 Till then, the petitioner shall not be arrested in connection with FIR No.376/2017, Police Station Sumerpur, Pali.\"",
    "arguments": "3. At the outset, learned counsel for the petitioner submits that on earlier times, the petitioners were working with the main accused Kamlesh Kumar and Vitthal Kumar and another persons. 4. Learned counsel for the petitioner states that the interim order has already operating in favour of the petitioners and they are both real brothers and in fact on bare perusal of the FIR, the offence is not made out. 5. Learned counsel for the petitioners states that the petitioners want to submit a representation alongwith all the relevant documents before the concerned investigating authority.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. At the outset, learned counsel for the petitioner submits that on earlier times, the petitioners were working with the main accused Kamlesh Kumar and Vitthal Kumar and another persons. 4. Learned counsel for the petitioner states that the interim order has already operating in favour of the petitioners and they are both real brothers and in fact on bare perusal of the FIR, the offence is not made out.",
    "respondent_arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the petitioners states that the petitioners want to submit a representation alongwith all the relevant documents before the concerned investigating authority.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
